title: The Siege of Wesel
subtitle: The fortress guns are killing our men by the dozen.
view-if: crisis_ruhr = 1 and e20_ruhr_front_done = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; e20_ruhr_front_done = 1
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= The Siege of Wesel

The Red Army's units elect their commanders in the pits and the steelworks. Some men go home every night to sleep. Before Wesel, where the Reichswehr holds the Rhine crossing, the army's guns have the range of every trench.

- @storm: Storm Wesel.
- @dig: Lift the siege and dig in along the Lippe.

@storm
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Perhaps one chance in three. The bridge would cut Watter off from the Rhineland.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.e20_wesel = Math.random() < 0.4 ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.e20_wesel) { Q.e20_ruhr_towns += 2; Q.e20_ruhr_watter -= 4; }
else { Q.e20_ruhr_men = Math.max(5, Q.e20_ruhr_men - 8); }
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
Q.crisis_line_1 = 'Towns held: ' + Q.e20_ruhr_towns;
Q.crisis_line_2 = 'Red Army: ' + Q.e20_ruhr_men + ',000 men';
Q.crisis_line_3 = 'Watter\'s troops at Münster: ' + Q.e20_ruhr_watter + ',000';
!}

[? if e20_wesel = 1 : The fortress falls to a night assault across the canal. The Red Army has the guns of Wesel and the bridge. ?][? if e20_wesel = 0 : The assault breaks down under machine-gun fire before the walls. Hundreds of miners lie dead in the fields outside the town. ?]

@dig
subtitle: The front will give less ground when Watter comes.
on-arrival: e20_ruhr_dug = 1; lean_unionist += 1

The men grumble about the spades. Fewer of them die.
